Strings    : The 35 web i18n keys (mapOverview.* + error.loadFailed) are resolved in code through the
             ILocalizer facade with the verbatim web key names and the web English defaults
             (MapOverviewStrings.Resolve). 33 of the 35 are ALREADY present in the platform catalog
             apps/windows/Strings/{en,he,ar}/Resources.resw (harvested from MapOverviewPage.tsx by the
             cross-platform i18n generator); the remaining two — mapOverview.noHistory and mapOverview.subtitle
             — are not yet harvested (the web defines them only as inline t() defaults, so the generator emitted
             no row), and the page falls back to the same English default the web uses, via ShellLocalizer ->
             Localization.Get. The .resw is generator-owned ("AUTO-GENERATED … do not edit by hand"), is NOT
             referenced by TeslaSync.App.csproj (so it never enters the build), and is already malformed at HEAD
             (multiple unclosed <data> tags, e.g. translation.admin.auditLog.verifying, unrelated to this page);
             it was therefore left untouched rather than hand-patched. All 35 keys are asserted resolved
             headlessly (MapOverviewPageTests, PassthroughLocalizer), and the page contains zero hardcoded
             visible literals.

Files:
  feature-views/MapOverviewPage/MapOverviewPage.Model.cs      (records + parsers + projection + registration + diagnostics + strings + feed port)
  feature-views/MapOverviewPage/MapOverviewPage.Source.cs     (generated C# client reads: GET /vehicles ; /vehicles/{vehicleID}/positions?limit ; /location-snapshots/latest?vehicle_id)
  feature-views/MapOverviewPage/MapOverviewPage.ViewModel.cs  (INotifyPropertyChanged 4-state holder + vehicle selection + map style + 15s latest auto-refresh + units)
  feature-views/MapOverviewPage/MapOverviewPage.cs            (WinUI 3 UserControl, Fluent + design tokens; TsPageContainer scaffold + map/playback/cards/details/quick-links/history)
  TeslaSync.App.Tests/FeatureViews/MapOverviewPageTests.cs    (37 headless tests)
  TeslaSync.App.Tests/TeslaSync.App.Tests.csproj              (link the 3 UI-free files; the WinUI view is build-only)

Data sources (P1/S8 ObservableObject VM → generated C# client, web hook/query names kept at the C# call sites):
  useVehicles                                   -> MapOverviewClientFeed.FetchVehiclesAsync, ApiRequest(Operations.Vehicles.List).
  useQuery(['position-latest', id])  limit=1    -> FetchLatestPositionAsync, ApiRequest(Operations.Vehicles.Positions){vehicleID}{limit=1}.
  useQuery(['position-history', id]) limit=50   -> FetchPositionHistoryAsync, ApiRequest(Operations.Vehicles.Positions){vehicleID}{limit=50}.
  useQuery(['location-latest', id])             -> FetchLocationSnapshotAsync, ApiRequest(Operations.Locations.SnapshotLatest){vehicle_id}.
  (The manifest declares only useVehicles as a *named* hook; the web page genuinely performs the three inline
   position/location reads — required by the 9 panels + 7 maps + the 4 declared data states — so all four are
   bound and loading/empty/error/success are real, not faked. The web location-snapshot query's failure is NOT
   folded into anyError, so MapOverviewPageViewModel swallows it — ViewModel_swallows_location_snapshot_failure.)
Units (P1/S5): SI read from the API; converted ONLY at the display boundary in MapOverviewProjection via
  UnitConverters.SpeedFromSi / DistanceFromSi + ScalarFormatters (speed m/s -> km/h|mph; odometer m -> km|mi).
  Note: the web Odometer row renders raw odometer (a latent missing-conversion); the native port applies the
  binding SI-boundary conversion (frontend-si-cutover) so the value is correct beside its distance-unit label —
  asserted by Odometer_converts_to_imperial_miles. lat/lon/heading are geographic/dimensionless (unconverted).
Live data: the web page is TanStack-Query polling (refetchInterval 15_000 on the latest position), not SSE, so
  there is no live SSE subscription / >2-min staleness chip beyond the header TsDataFreshness chip (ADR-013 live
  path n/a). The 15s latest auto-refresh is ported as a DispatcherTimer -> ViewModel.RefreshLatestAsync
  (ViewModel_refresh_latest_refetches_only_the_latest_position). When no vehicle is selected the page shows the
  shared NoVehicleSelected onboarding surface (web early return) — No_vehicle_guard_when_resolved_without_a_selection.

